        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(durable): hand off wakes to session queue",
        "body": "# PR5/5 - internal session delivery handoff + final hardening\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThis finishes the beta3 durable-core stack by turning resolved durable wake\nobligations into an internal session delivery-queue handoff on gateway startup.\nAfter PR4 made wakes inspectable and controllable, PR5 gives the durable runtime\na concrete recovery path: a resolved wake is replayed, persisted with delivery\nevidence, and queued for the owning OpenClaw session without inventing external\nchannel sends.\n\n## Stack position\n\n- Stack item: PR5/5\n- Clean PR5 comparison: `a30e2b6ce4e5f1390599380aedc82078c98854f7..443ffd2292e146fad3c089a03382a5f4702632f7`\n- PR4 dependency: `https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/105844`\n- GitHub base rationale: existing PR1-PR4 stack PRs target `release/2026.7.1`; the PR4 branch exists on the fork, not as an upstream base branch, so this PR follows stack convention while documenting the exact PR4-head diff.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Adds `createDurableWakeSessionDeliveryHook`, which resolves durable wakes to\n  agent/session keys and enqueues one internal `systemEvent` via the session\n  delivery queue.\n- Wires gateway startup durable wake replay through that hook.\n- Persists delivery evidence with `internalDelivery: \"session_delivery_queue\"`\n  and `noExternalSend: true`.\n- Extends focused replay/startup tests for idempotency, startup replay, ambiguous\n  target handling, and no autonomous resume/abandon/create-new policy.\n- Updates durable docs to clarify the `delivered` state and CLI wake-attempt\n  evidence.\n\n## Non-scope\n\n- No Discord, Signal, Slack, plugin, or other external transport delivery is\n  implemented or claimed.\n- No cron mutation.\n- No release/changelog/package churn from the stale old PR5 ancestry.\n- No broad durable orchestration policy changes beyond this internal handoff.\n\n## Evidence\n\nClean scope:\n\n```text\n6 files changed, 372 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)\n```\n\nFocused behavior:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/durable/wake-delivery-replay.test.ts src/durable/startup.test.ts\n# pass: 2 files, 14 tests\n```\n\nAdjacent durable CLI/Gateway/read-path proof:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/durable.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts src/durable/wake-controls-inspection.test.ts\n# pass: 3 Vitest shards, 4 files, 25 tests\n```\n\nStatic/docs gates:\n\n```bash\npnpm check:test-types\n# pass\n\npnpm check:docs\n# pass\n\ngit diff --check a30e2b6ce4e5f1390599380aedc82078c98854f7..HEAD\n# pass\n```\n\nRemote proof attempts were made but unavailable in this shell:\n\n```text\nblacksmith-testbox: blocked, blacksmith CLI not found in PATH\naws Crabbox: blocked, broker login missing\n```\n\n## Upgrade contract\n\nThis PR adds no schema migration. It writes wake delivery attempts using the\nexisting durable wake attempt ledger and queues internal session deliveries using\nthe existing session delivery queue idempotency contract. Repeated startup replay\nmust not duplicate queued events once a wake is marked delivered.\n\n## Risk / limits\n\n- Main risk is semantic: reviewers should confirm `delivered` remains scoped to\n  internal durable/session handoff and cannot be mistaken for external channel\n  transport success.\n- Remote Testbox proof is still desirable before merge because local provider\n  setup blocked it here.\n- Full release validation was not run for this narrow PR5 slice.\n\n@clawsweeper review\n",
        "branch": "codex/openclaw-durable-beta3-newstack-pr5-session-handoff-final-v2",
